module

public import Theory.Representation.AlternatingSevenBinaryLargeModels.Fourteen
import Mathlib.Tactic

/-!
# Absolute irreducibility of the binary fourteen-space

The certificate starts with the identity and successively left-multiplies earlier
matrices by the actions of (0 1 2) and (0 1 2 3 4 5 6). Its 196 matrices span the
full matrix algebra: an explicit binary inverse table expresses each matrix unit.
Every multiplication and inverse-table identity is checked by kernel reduction of
packed XOR computations, using the soundness lemmas in `PackedDensity`.

The companion `Absolute` module uses these identities to prove matrix density
and absolute irreducibility without assuming a representation catalogue. Together
they supply the fourteen-space construction used in Aschbacher–Smith K.1.2
(printed p.452/PDF p.463).
-/

